{
  "experiment": "ERA on AgentDescent -- LLM-SRBench, what each root node is worth before any LLM",
  "why": "The benchmark ships no program, so every method brings its own starting point and a comparison with the paper's tables depends on which one. `library` is this port's root -- sparse regression over a fixed nonlinear basis. `linear` is LLM-SR's own starting point, a fitted linear model in the raw inputs (methods/llmsr/searcher.py), transcribed into this port's contract. No LLM is involved in any number below.",
  "finding": "On LSR-Synth the root alone is worth 45 points of Acc(0.1) -- 48.1% against 3.1% -- so this port's LSR-Synth results are mostly the root rather than the search. On LSR-Transform both roots are worthless (0.9% against 0.0%), so the per-problem result there was earned by the search.",
